 "about_text": "Gabba Gallery is a contemporary art gallery in Los Angeles that has been open since 2012, showing work by emerging and established artists from around the world with a strong emphasis on street art, graffiti-rooted practice, and mixed-media painting. Founded by Jason Ostro, who named the space after his late father's nickname for him, the gallery spent eleven years in Historic Filipinotown on Beverly Blvd before relocating to 235 S. Broadway in Downtown Los Angeles. Beyond its exhibition program, Gabba runs the Gabba Alley Project, bringing murals and public art into surrounding neighborhoods to foster community engagement.",
